 "scenery": [],
 "par": {
  "time": 660
 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "ASH BASILICA",
  "lines": [
   "A house of the Song, burned out and kept.",
   "Five stations, five rooms. At each one, someone who wants the Grafting to go on."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Behind the altar a stair goes down. The ash on it has been walked by many feet, all going the same way.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [31, 66],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Ash on the flags and soot to the roof. Everything that can burn has. The stone is still warm at the foot of the walls."
  },
  {
   "id": "raised",
   "at": [31, 58],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "There are galleries two metres up in most of these rooms, with stairs at their ends. High ground costs a flight of steps and gives you the room below."
  },
  {
   "id": "haul",
   "at": [24, 57],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "First station, THE HAUL. Run a nail down it: the line is drawn in, hand over hand, by all of the ones who are able. It is owed."
  },
  {
   "id": "slip",
   "at": [17, 55],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Haul, hold, chock, fit, float. That's a launch. Five stages, in that order, on every slip I ever stood beside. They are launching something here."
  },
  {
   "id": "hold",
   "at": [14, 46],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Second station, THE HOLD. The line is made fast. It is not lost if it is held: the Mother holds it, and weeps, and does not let go."
  },
  {
   "id": "chock",
   "at": [27, 40],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Third station, THE CHOCK. A wedge is set and the wheel is stopped. The wheel is a person who has been asked to stand still."
  },
  {
   "id": "fit",
   "at": [32, 26],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Fourth station, THE FIT. The bell is fitted. A rank of the willing holds the one who is being fitted, so that it is done without fear."
  },
  {
   "id": "zealot",
   "at": [35, 23],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Spears in a rank, shoulder to shoulder, facing the far screen with their backs to me. They guard the one behind them from the ones in front."
  },
  {
   "id": "float",
   "at": [58, 14],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Fifth station, THE FLOAT. The first toll. After it the fitted one is no longer asked anything, because it has been answered."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [14, 60],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The wall behind the west gallery rings hollow where a plate has been taken down."
  },
  {
   "id": "crypt",
   "at": [14, 64],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "The ones of this house who would not be fitted are put here. Their bells are on the wall, unfitted, in a row. Take what they left."
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "at": [38, 40],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The wall at the end of this arm has cracked in the heat, and there is a cell behind it. One shot would finish it."
  },
  {
   "id": "found",
   "at": [43, 40],
   "radius": 1.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A sexton's cell. Rivets with hard points, a mend, and a blanket folded on a stone bed."
  },
  {
   "id": "altar",
   "at": [37, 9],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "An organ with no pipes left but the lowest ones, and the lowest are warm. Somebody is still playing this house. Very slowly. One note a minute."
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Fight through the house, station by station. Each screen opens when the ones who hold it are dead",
